---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Daily AI Notes keeps about you, why, and for how long.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="label">Privacy</div>
    <h1 class="h1">What we keep, and for how long</h1>
  </header>
  <div class="measure stack">
    <p>
      Daily AI Notes is a small open-source project. It keeps as little as it can, sells nothing and
      runs no advertising or tracking scripts. The code that does all of this is public on{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/erentnr/dailyainotes">GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <section class="section stack">
      <div class="label">Without an account</div>
      <p>
        The topics you pick stay in your browser. The site asks for the notes on them, but does not
        store which topics anyone follows.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you ask the notes a question, we keep the question, the notes the answer cited, and a
        keyed hash of your IP address that cannot be turned back into the address, for 30 days. The
        hash also counts your questions for the day's limit; those counts are deleted after a day.
      </p>
      <p>Our server logs record requests without IP addresses or request headers.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section stack">
      <div class="label">With an account</div>
      <p>
        Your email address, the topics you follow, the topics you suggest, and your sign-in sessions.
        A session is a random token in a cookie that scripts cannot read; we store only a hash of it,
        with when it was made and last used, and it ends after 30 days without use. Sign-in codes
        are stored as hashes too, and deleted once they expire.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can delete your account on your <a href="/account">account page</a> at any time. That
        removes all of it at once.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section stack">
      <div class="label">Who else sees what</div>
      <ul class="stack">
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> carries every request to this site, and its Turnstile check on
          the sign-in form tells people from bots.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> sends the sign-in email, so it receives your address and the code.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ollama Cloud</strong> runs the model that answers Ask, so it receives your question
          with the notes that answer it. It says it does not log or train on what it is sent.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Langfuse</strong> records each model call, including Ask questions, so we can see
          how the pipeline behaves; it keeps them for 30 days.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section stack">
      <div class="label">Questions</div>
      <p>
        Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/erentnr/dailyainotes/issues">GitHub</a>, without
        personal details; we will reply there.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
